course: dictionary
lesson: 5696
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. The word loft can mean the space under a roof, a shed for birds, or a high kick or hit. In «A homing pigeon let out a hundred kilometres from its loft flies back», the word pigeon is the clue, so a loft here must be a shed where pigeons live.
explain: Look at the words around loft to decide. In «Thick walls, fluffy loft insulation and double windows slow heat leaking out of a house», insulation and heat leaking out of a house tell you a loft is the space under the roof of a house. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Loft can also be a doing word. A player lofts the ball over a defender, which means she hits or kicks it high into the air. Ask who is doing the action and what is being moved. Those clues show you which meaning fits.
fact: A loft is the room or space just under the roof of a house, often used for storage.
fact: A pigeon loft is a shed for keeping pigeons.
fact: A hayloft is the upper floor of a barn where hay is stored.
fact: To loft a ball is to hit or kick it high into the air.
fact: Pipes in lofts are wrapped in foam lagging, so a loft is a place in a house where pipes are kept.
exercise: «A homing pigeon let out a hundred kilometres from its loft flies back as if it had a map and compass inside its head.» In this sentence, what is a loft? | A high kick in football | *A shed where pigeons live | A large flat in an old factory | The top floor of a bus
exercise: «Thick walls, fluffy loft insulation and double windows slow heat leaking out of a house.» What is the loft in this sentence? | A sports pitch | A shed for pigeons | *The space just under the roof of a house | A large flat in an old factory
exercise: A player lofts the ball over a defender. What does lofts mean? | Drops it on the ground | *Hits or kicks it high into the air | Hides it under a blanket | Rolls it along the grass
test: In «A homing pigeon let out a hundred kilometres from its loft flies back», what does loft mean? | The top floor of a barn | To kick a ball high | The space under a roof where toys are kept | *A shed for keeping pigeons
test: Which word from the lesson means to hit or kick a ball high into the air? | *Loft | Insulation | Pigeon | Lagging
exam: In «The old toys are stored up in the loft», which meaning fits best? | A shed for keeping pigeons | A large flat in an old factory | To hit a ball high into the air | *The space under the roof of a house, used for storage
